{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineY"},{"type":"text","value":" draws horizontal profiles above categorical y baselines.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes the contract and extends vertical profiles to the right\nof categorical x baselines."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ridgelineY } from '@tanstack/charts/ridgeline'\n\nconst mark = ridgelineY(profileRows, {\n  x: 'x',\n  y: 'category',\n  height: 'height',\n  overlap: 0.8,\n  color: 'category',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both marks are also exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/universal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prepared-profiles","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prepared profiles"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark lays out prepared profile samples. It does not bin observations,\nestimate a density, or normalize values. Keep those decisions visible with\ntransforms or application data preparation."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const bins = binX(rows, {\n  value: 'rating',\n  by: 'season',\n  thresholds: boundaries,\n  outputs: { count: { reduce: 'count' } },\n})\nconst profiles = normalize(bins, {\n  value: 'count',\n  by: 'season',\n  basis: 'max',\n  as: 'height',\n})\n\ndefineChart({\n  marks: [\n    ridgelineY(profiles, {\n      x: 'x',\n      y: 'season',\n      height: 'height',\n      overlap: 0.78,\n      color: 'season',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleLinear().domain([4, 10]) },\n    y: {\n      scale: scalePoint<number>().domain(seasons).padding(0.78),\n      reverse: true,\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" must be finite and within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[0, 1]"},{"type":"text","value":". Nullish and nonfinite profile\npositions or heights create gaps. Sort samples into the intended profile order\nbefore passing them to the mark."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"signatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ridgelineY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: RidgelineYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction ridgelineX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: RidgelineXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The profile position is numeric or temporal. The category is a numeric or\nstring "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public type surface includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RidgelinePosition"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RidgelineCurve"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RidgelineStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RidgelineYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RidgelineXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number | Date?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by Y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Horizontal profile position for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineY"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by Y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categorical baseline for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineY"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categorical baseline for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number | Date?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required by X"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vertical profile position for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normalized displacement from the category baseline"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overlap"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Peak displacement in category-step units"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable profile-sample identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value sent to the chart color scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category profile paint; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke: null"},{"type":"text","value":" omits the outline"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Area and outline presentation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outline dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"curve"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RidgelineCurve"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Straight"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer-neutral profile path generator"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-driven opacity styles shared by area and outline"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyed area and outline motion policy"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overlap"},{"type":"text","value":" must be positive and finite. A value of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" reaches the next category\nbaseline, values below "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" leave space, and values above "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" overlap adjacent\nprofiles."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"category-scale-and-padding","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category scale and padding"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The categorical axis must resolve to a point or band scale. Ridge displacement\nuses the smallest step in the complete configured domain, including categories\nwithout profile rows. This keeps geometry stable when a category is empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Point-scale padding controls room outside the first and last baseline. Set its\npadding to at least "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overlap"},{"type":"text","value":" when peaks must remain inside the plot. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reverse: true"},{"type":"text","value":" on a y scale when the first authored category should appear at\nthe bottom."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categories paint in first-occurrence order; each category's area paints before\nall outlines. Source order therefore controls which profile is on top when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overlap"},{"type":"text","value":" exceeds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"identity-and-interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identity and interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each valid sample contributes one semantic interaction point even though the\nmark paints both an area and an outline. The point retains the exact source\ndatum and index. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineY"},{"type":"text","value":" reports the profile position as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xValue"},{"type":"text","value":" and the\ncategory as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yValue"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ridgelineX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Profile areas and outlines share the same points, focus affinity, state opacity,\nand keyed motion. Use an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" when positions repeat within a category."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"prepared-profiles","text":"Prepared profiles","level":2},{"id":"signatures","text":"Signatures","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"category-scale-and-padding","text":"Category scale and padding","level":2},{"id":"identity-and-interaction","text":"Identity and interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`ridgelineY` draws horizontal profiles above categorical y baselines.\n`ridgelineX` transposes the contract and extends vertical profiles to the right\nof categorical x baselines.\n\n```ts\nimport { ridgelineY } from '@tanstack/charts/ridgeline'\n\nconst mark = ridgelineY(profileRows, {\n  x: 'x',\n  y: 'category',\n  height: 'height',\n  overlap: 0.8,\n  color: 'category',\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Prepared profiles\n\nThe mark lays out prepared profile samples. It does not bin observations,\nestimate a density, or normalize values. Keep those decisions visible with\ntransforms or application data preparation.\n\n```ts\nconst bins = binX(rows, {\n  value: 'rating',\n  by: 'season',\n  thresholds: boundaries,\n  outputs: { count: { reduce: 'count' } },\n})\nconst profiles = normalize(bins, {\n  value: 'count',\n  by: 'season',\n  basis: 'max',\n  as: 'height',\n})\n\ndefineChart({\n  marks: [\n    ridgelineY(profiles, {\n      x: 'x',\n      y: 'season',\n      height: 'height',\n      overlap: 0.78,\n      color: 'season',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleLinear().domain([4, 10]) },\n    y: {\n      scale: scalePoint<number>().domain(seasons).padding(0.78),\n      reverse: true,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`height` must be finite and within `[0, 1]`. Nullish and nonfinite profile\npositions or heights create gaps. Sort samples into the intended profile order\nbefore passing them to the mark.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction ridgelineY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: RidgelineYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction ridgelineX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: RidgelineXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n```\n\nThe profile position is numeric or temporal. The category is a numeric or\nstring `ChartKey`.\n\nThe public type surface includes `RidgelinePosition`, `RidgelineCurve`,\n`RidgelineStateStyle`, `RidgelineYOptions`, and `RidgelineXOptions`.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                       | Default          | Meaning                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by Y    | Horizontal profile position for `ridgelineY`             |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by Y    | Categorical baseline for `ridgelineY`                    |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by X    | Categorical baseline for `ridgelineX`                    |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by X    | Vertical profile position for `ridgelineX`               |\n| `height`                                          | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required         | Normalized displacement from the category baseline       |\n| `overlap`                                         | `number`                                   | `1`              | Peak displacement in category-step units                 |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                   | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                           |\n| `key`                                             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred         | Stable profile-sample identity                           |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Category         | Value sent to the chart color scale                      |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                                  | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`            | Resolved color   | Category profile paint; `stroke: null` omits the outline |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                   | Renderer default | Area and outline presentation                            |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                   | None             | Outline dash pattern                                     |\n| `curve`                                           | `RidgelineCurve`                           | Straight         | Renderer-neutral profile path generator                  |\n| `states`                                          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                | None             | Focus-driven opacity styles shared by area and outline   |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']` | None             | Keyed area and outline motion policy                     |\n\n`overlap` must be positive and finite. A value of `1` reaches the next category\nbaseline, values below `1` leave space, and values above `1` overlap adjacent\nprofiles.\n\n## Category scale and padding\n\nThe categorical axis must resolve to a point or band scale. Ridge displacement\nuses the smallest step in the complete configured domain, including categories\nwithout profile rows. This keeps geometry stable when a category is empty.\n\nPoint-scale padding controls room outside the first and last baseline. Set its\npadding to at least `overlap` when peaks must remain inside the plot. Use\n`reverse: true` on a y scale when the first authored category should appear at\nthe bottom.\n\nCategories paint in first-occurrence order; each category's area paints before\nall outlines. Source order therefore controls which profile is on top when\n`overlap` exceeds `1`.\n\n## Identity and interaction\n\nEach valid sample contributes one semantic interaction point even though the\nmark paints both an area and an outline. The point retains the exact source\ndatum and index. `ridgelineY` reports the profile position as `xValue` and the\ncategory as `yValue`; `ridgelineX` transposes them.\n\nProfile areas and outlines share the same points, focus affinity, state opacity,\nand keyed motion. Use an explicit `key` when positions repeat within a category.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Ridgeline Marks\ndescription: Reference for semantic ridgelineY and ridgelineX profile geometry, categorical baselines, overlap, curves, identity, and interaction.\n---\n\n`ridgelineY` draws horizontal profiles above categorical y baselines.\n`ridgelineX` transposes the contract and extends vertical profiles to the right\nof categorical x baselines.\n\n```ts\nimport { ridgelineY } from '@tanstack/charts/ridgeline'\n\nconst mark = ridgelineY(profileRows, {\n  x: 'x',\n  y: 'category',\n  height: 'height',\n  overlap: 0.8,\n  color: 'category',\n})\n```\n\nBoth marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Prepared profiles\n\nThe mark lays out prepared profile samples. It does not bin observations,\nestimate a density, or normalize values. Keep those decisions visible with\ntransforms or application data preparation.\n\n```ts\nconst bins = binX(rows, {\n  value: 'rating',\n  by: 'season',\n  thresholds: boundaries,\n  outputs: { count: { reduce: 'count' } },\n})\nconst profiles = normalize(bins, {\n  value: 'count',\n  by: 'season',\n  basis: 'max',\n  as: 'height',\n})\n\ndefineChart({\n  marks: [\n    ridgelineY(profiles, {\n      x: 'x',\n      y: 'season',\n      height: 'height',\n      overlap: 0.78,\n      color: 'season',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleLinear().domain([4, 10]) },\n    y: {\n      scale: scalePoint<number>().domain(seasons).padding(0.78),\n      reverse: true,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n`height` must be finite and within `[0, 1]`. Nullish and nonfinite profile\npositions or heights create gaps. Sort samples into the intended profile order\nbefore passing them to the mark.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction ridgelineY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: RidgelineYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n\nfunction ridgelineX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: RidgelineXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum>\n```\n\nThe profile position is numeric or temporal. The category is a numeric or\nstring `ChartKey`.\n\nThe public type surface includes `RidgelinePosition`, `RidgelineCurve`,\n`RidgelineStateStyle`, `RidgelineYOptions`, and `RidgelineXOptions`.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option                                            | Type                                       | Default          | Meaning                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by Y    | Horizontal profile position for `ridgelineY`             |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by Y    | Categorical baseline for `ridgelineY`                    |\n| `x`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Required by X    | Categorical baseline for `ridgelineX`                    |\n| `y`                                               | `Channel<TDatum, number \\| Date?>`         | Required by X    | Vertical profile position for `ridgelineX`               |\n| `height`                                          | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`                 | Required         | Normalized displacement from the category baseline       |\n| `overlap`                                         | `number`                                   | `1`              | Peak displacement in category-step units                 |\n| `id`                                              | `string`                                   | Layer-derived    | Stable mark ID                                           |\n| `key`                                             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                | Inferred         | Stable profile-sample identity                           |\n| `color`                                           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`               | Category         | Value sent to the chart color scale                      |\n| `fill`, `stroke`                                  | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`            | Resolved color   | Category profile paint; `stroke: null` omits the outline |\n| `fillOpacity`, `strokeOpacity`, and `strokeWidth` | `number`                                   | Renderer default | Area and outline presentation                            |\n| `strokeDasharray`                                 | `string`                                   | None             | Outline dash pattern                                     |\n| `curve`                                           | `RidgelineCurve`                           | Straight         | Renderer-neutral profile path generator                  |\n| `states`                                          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`                | None             | Focus-driven opacity styles shared by area and outline   |\n| `motion`                                          | `ChartMarkMotionOptions<TDatum>['motion']` | None             | Keyed area and outline motion policy                     |\n\n`overlap` must be positive and finite. A value of `1` reaches the next category\nbaseline, values below `1` leave space, and values above `1` overlap adjacent\nprofiles.\n\n## Category scale and padding\n\nThe categorical axis must resolve to a point or band scale. Ridge displacement\nuses the smallest step in the complete configured domain, including categories\nwithout profile rows. This keeps geometry stable when a category is empty.\n\nPoint-scale padding controls room outside the first and last baseline. Set its\npadding to at least `overlap` when peaks must remain inside the plot. Use\n`reverse: true` on a y scale when the first authored category should appear at\nthe bottom.\n\nCategories paint in first-occurrence order; each category's area paints before\nall outlines. Source order therefore controls which profile is on top when\n`overlap` exceeds `1`.\n\n## Identity and interaction\n\nEach valid sample contributes one semantic interaction point even though the\nmark paints both an area and an outline. The point retains the exact source\ndatum and index. `ridgelineY` reports the profile position as `xValue` and the\ncategory as `yValue`; `ridgelineX` transposes them.\n\nProfile areas and outlines share the same points, focus affinity, state opacity,\nand keyed motion. Use an explicit `key` when positions repeat within a category.\n"}
